ck options. Moves like (E, 3) flip internal pieces, which would grant the opponent more tactical opportunities.\n\nReason: By selecting (C, 7), I adhere to the strategy of minimizing flipped discs (mobility maximization) and avoiding the exposure of internal pieces. This keeps the board tight and forces the opponent into a potentially weaker position, while (E, 3) and (C, 3) would volatilize the center of the board too early.\n\nAnswer: (C, 7)'}
